  "findings": {
    "spontaneous_silence": "Exactly 0 spikes in 30/30 trials on the signed run-006 subgraph: no endogenous activity. Clean-control property - all downstream activity is attributable to injected drive. (Same result as run-005's silent baseline, now on the biologically signed graph.)",
    "stimulus_response_bounded": "DNge104-pair drive: 298.8 +- 20.6 spikes/s in exactly 2 spiking neurons (the seeds). GABAergic suppression signature (WP6b) holds at benchmark scale: drive confined to seeds, latency 3.4 +- 2.5 ms, peak population rate 219.3 +- 22.9 Hz.",
    "circuit_propagation_cliff": "hop 0 (seeds) = 2 spikers; ALL deeper hops = 0 spikers in 30/30 trials. Unlike run-005's INVALIDATED structural zero, run-006 is a depth-2 closure where second-order neurons exist (first-order targets are present in the node set), so this cliff is a genuine measurement: inhibitory seeds do not recruit. GABA/glutamate-mediated suppression prevents cascade propagation.",
    "sugar_recruitment_bounded": "17 sugar GRNs driven at 200 Hz recruit 411.5 +- 9.4 neurons (1.02% of 40,290) at 17,590 +- 368 spikes/s network-wide, peak population rate 49.7 Hz. First excitatory recruitment benchmark: cholinergic sensory drive produces bounded, local recruitment - no cascade - on the signed graph.",
    "cross_run_consistency": "run-006 stimulus_response (298.8 spikes/s, 2 spikers) matches WP6b's independent 30-trial measurement (308/2 in ours, 299/2 in the reference arm) - benchmark machinery and validation runs agree on the signed graph."
